        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 5:44PM CDT by NWS Norman OK</headline>
        <description>At 544 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 10
miles north of Avard, moving northeast at 35 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects.

This storm will remain over mainly rural areas of northeastern Woods
County west and northwest of Alva and Capron.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
